WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:03.797
- Something magical happens
when you do what you love.

00:00:03.797 --> 00:00:05.789
I hate lazy people, I hate laziness,

00:00:05.789 --> 00:00:07.789
I just don't like procrastination.

00:00:07.789 --> 00:00:09.180
I don't like people that make up excuses.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:12.390
I was always like, when I
do it, I'ma do it right.

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:13.557
When I do it, I'ma do it big.

00:00:13.557 --> 00:00:16.338
In a way, I always felt
like it was my calling

00:00:16.338 --> 00:00:18.137
to do something bigger than just be

00:00:18.137 --> 00:00:20.191
in Southside Jamaica, Queens hanging out.

00:00:20.191 --> 00:00:21.732
I think that being an underground artist

00:00:21.732 --> 00:00:24.125
was the best thing I could
have ever done in my life.

00:00:24.125 --> 00:00:26.333
You have to be a beast.

00:00:26.333 --> 00:00:28.541
That's the only way they respect you.

00:00:28.541 --> 00:00:29.742
Everybody's not going to like Nicki Minaj.

00:00:29.742 --> 00:00:31.372
You know what I mean?

00:00:31.372 --> 00:00:33.110
Everybody's not going
to like the way I look.

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:35.213
- She's a Trinidad-born American rapper,

00:00:35.213 --> 00:00:36.623
singer, and songwriter.

00:00:36.623 --> 00:00:37.536
She was the first female artist

00:00:37.536 --> 00:00:41.325
to be listed on MTV's
annual Hottest MC list.

00:00:41.325 --> 00:00:43.893
In 2016, she was listed on Time Magazine's

00:00:43.893 --> 00:00:46.526
Most Influential Hundred
People in the World.

00:00:46.526 --> 00:00:48.194
She's Nicki Minaj, and here's my take

00:00:48.194 --> 00:00:50.042
on her top ten rules for success.

00:00:50.042 --> 00:00:51.616
Number ten is my personal favorite,

00:00:51.616 --> 00:00:53.278
I'd make sure to stick
around all the way to the end

00:00:53.278 --> 00:00:55.256
for some special bonus clips.

00:00:55.256 --> 00:00:58.016
(jets blasting)

00:00:58.016 --> 00:00:58.849
- Be you.

00:01:01.515 --> 00:01:05.062
Make sure that your art isn't being done

00:01:05.062 --> 00:01:06.395
to please anyone

00:01:07.328 --> 00:01:08.161
but you,

00:01:09.318 --> 00:01:13.485
because something magical happens
when you do what you love,

00:01:14.367 --> 00:01:18.136
and whether it's loved
by the masses or not,

00:01:18.136 --> 00:01:22.136
there's magic in that
genuine love that you have

00:01:23.109 --> 00:01:26.876
for your own art, and it
could never be taken away.

00:01:26.876 --> 00:01:29.976
And little by little,
people start catching on.

00:01:29.976 --> 00:01:32.999
So just follow your heart
and don't be afraid.

00:01:32.999 --> 00:01:35.715
Really I just kept at it.

00:01:35.715 --> 00:01:39.437
I work, work, work, work,
work, I don't believe in...

00:01:39.437 --> 00:01:41.473
I hate lazy people, I hate laziness,

00:01:41.473 --> 00:01:43.297
I just don't like procrastination,

00:01:43.297 --> 00:01:45.819
I don't like people that make
up excuses, just get it done.

00:01:45.819 --> 00:01:48.042
And I've always taken
that approach with my life

00:01:48.042 --> 00:01:52.172
and my career, and I guess
that's why I've been around.

00:01:52.172 --> 00:01:54.731
And I haven't just
gotten around, you know?

00:01:54.731 --> 00:01:57.700
I've been here for a minute.
(Nicki and Guy crosstalk)

00:01:57.700 --> 00:01:59.199
So I've been trying for a long time

00:01:59.199 --> 00:02:01.725
and it just goes to show you
if you really want something,

00:02:01.725 --> 00:02:03.375
you work hard at it, you
know what I'm saying,

00:02:03.375 --> 00:02:04.465
eventually people will come around.

00:02:04.465 --> 00:02:06.995
It's just up to you to stick with it.

00:02:06.995 --> 00:02:09.435
I think the problem is a
lot of people just give up

00:02:09.435 --> 00:02:11.602
because it's so difficult.

00:02:12.668 --> 00:02:15.565
It's like, you got bills to pay (mumbles),

00:02:15.565 --> 00:02:17.575
you got to do this, so a
lot of people just give up,

00:02:17.575 --> 00:02:19.932
but I just didn't; I just kept working.

00:02:19.932 --> 00:02:23.427
It's a ladder, you want to
climb the ladder to success.

00:02:23.427 --> 00:02:28.028
Some people don't appreciate
the first two or three steps.

00:02:28.028 --> 00:02:28.861
You know what I'm saying?

00:02:28.861 --> 00:02:30.976
They just want to get to the top.

00:02:30.976 --> 00:02:32.306
And...

00:02:32.306 --> 00:02:35.246
I always said, I didn't
want a rushed album,

00:02:35.246 --> 00:02:36.826
I didn't want to rush anything.

00:02:36.826 --> 00:02:38.936
I was always like,

00:02:38.936 --> 00:02:40.106
when I do it, I'ma do it right.

00:02:40.106 --> 00:02:43.094
When I do it, I'ma do it big.

00:02:43.094 --> 00:02:45.304
And a part of that is that grind,

00:02:45.304 --> 00:02:46.904
is the blood, sweat and tears,

00:02:46.904 --> 00:02:51.032
even though it doesn't feel
too good at the moment,

00:02:51.032 --> 00:02:53.023
I know that one day
I'ma look back and say,

00:02:53.023 --> 00:02:55.523
it was all worth it because...

00:02:57.163 --> 00:03:00.106
there's nothing better
than staying grounded

00:03:00.106 --> 00:03:02.026
and appreciating what you have.

00:03:02.026 --> 00:03:05.546
Cause even though I'm not
a multi-platinum artist,

00:03:05.546 --> 00:03:07.802
I know I'm still better
off than a lot of girls

00:03:07.802 --> 00:03:10.778
that have been trying to
do it for so many years,

00:03:10.778 --> 00:03:12.532
and they haven't gotten
their foot in the door,

00:03:12.532 --> 00:03:13.990
so, I'm their voice.

00:03:13.990 --> 00:03:16.933
You know, they probably hate
me, but I got love for them.

00:03:16.933 --> 00:03:18.556
And don't ever give up, I'm mean,

00:03:18.556 --> 00:03:20.705
I could have given up a million times

00:03:20.705 --> 00:03:24.729
and there's always something, you know,

00:03:24.729 --> 00:03:28.881
I guess in the back of my
head that just says, not yet.

00:03:28.881 --> 00:03:30.801
You should always listen to
that voice that tells you,

00:03:30.801 --> 00:03:33.571
not yet, don't give in just yet,

00:03:33.571 --> 00:03:35.531
because there's always
a billion people waiting

00:03:35.531 --> 00:03:37.125
to take your spot.

00:03:37.125 --> 00:03:39.455
And on another note,

00:03:39.455 --> 00:03:42.788
you don't know whose life you can touch

00:03:42.788 --> 00:03:44.543
when you do what you do.

00:03:44.543 --> 00:03:47.191
You know what I mean? So just
keep on doing your thing.

00:03:47.191 --> 00:03:49.441
- Dream Team Minaj says, "I
love you. But I'm curious,

00:03:49.441 --> 00:03:50.941
"why did you change your rapping style

00:03:50.941 --> 00:03:55.219
"from the come up days
to today? I love both."

00:03:55.219 --> 00:03:58.636
- I don't think I changed my rap style...

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:02.369
I think you guys were
just starting to hear me

00:04:02.369 --> 00:04:05.369
and you didn't hear all
of me yet, that's it.

00:04:05.369 --> 00:04:09.517
I've always been into
being weird a little bit.

00:04:09.517 --> 00:04:12.014
But I think what people
really mean is that

00:04:12.014 --> 00:04:15.347
they think that I've changed my persona.

00:04:16.669 --> 00:04:18.956
And life is about growth and change,

00:04:18.956 --> 00:04:23.264
and I don't want to remain
the same for my whole life.

00:04:23.264 --> 00:04:25.992
I want to be able to change,

00:04:25.992 --> 00:04:28.825
you know, I respect the people who

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:31.413
loved '07 Nicki,

00:04:32.525 --> 00:04:37.063
and I'm definitely going to give
you some stuff on Pink Friday.

00:04:37.063 --> 00:04:38.919
I'm not forgetting anybody,

00:04:38.919 --> 00:04:41.688
but I just also have to be true to me.

00:04:41.688 --> 00:04:45.784
And the truth is, I started
seeing different things.

00:04:45.784 --> 00:04:47.304
I started going different places.

00:04:47.304 --> 00:04:50.879
I started eating different things.

00:04:50.879 --> 00:04:54.421
It would be fraudulent
to rap the same way,

00:04:54.421 --> 00:04:55.701
and look the same way,
and act thee ame way,

00:04:55.701 --> 00:04:59.491
because I am not the
same, period, I'm not.

00:04:59.491 --> 00:05:01.624
Yeah, when I think
about where I came from,

00:05:01.624 --> 00:05:03.082
sometimes it is surprising.

00:05:03.082 --> 00:05:06.477
I guess, in a way, I always
felt like it was my calling

00:05:06.477 --> 00:05:08.282
to do something bigger than just be

00:05:08.282 --> 00:05:10.522
in Southside Jamaica, Queens hanging out.

00:05:10.522 --> 00:05:13.180
But, I guess every now and then,

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:15.467
I do feel like, wait a minute...

00:05:15.467 --> 00:05:16.627
Is this really my life?

00:05:16.627 --> 00:05:20.460
Like, I can't believe
I've impacted a culture,

00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:22.634
ya know, the hip-hop culture.

00:05:22.634 --> 00:05:24.974
Sometimes that is surreal for me because,

00:05:24.974 --> 00:05:28.587
I didn't even set out to be a
rapper. You know what I mean?

00:05:28.587 --> 00:05:29.420
You know like sometimes you have like

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:30.461
that dream when you're little?

00:05:30.461 --> 00:05:32.051
I didn't think when I
was like 10 years old,

00:05:32.051 --> 00:05:34.707
you know, I'ma be a
rapper one day. Ya know?

00:05:34.707 --> 00:05:39.281
It just happened, but
the other day I realized,

00:05:39.281 --> 00:05:42.538
even when things are bad or going crazy,

00:05:42.538 --> 00:05:44.168
I have so much to be thankful for.

00:05:44.168 --> 00:05:47.349
Those little tiny things that I have,

00:05:47.349 --> 00:05:51.053
like those people in my
life that I can count on,

00:05:51.053 --> 00:05:53.202
(exhales)

00:05:53.202 --> 00:05:54.035
You know what I mean?

00:05:54.035 --> 00:05:56.885
I can reflect now and be super
appreciative of everything.

00:05:56.885 --> 00:05:59.362
I think that being an underground
artist was the best thing

00:05:59.362 --> 00:06:01.492
I could have ever done in my life.

00:06:01.492 --> 00:06:02.942
Being independent and not signed

00:06:02.942 --> 00:06:05.403
to a major label was amazing because,

00:06:05.403 --> 00:06:09.148
ya know, it teaches you
to be your own boss.

00:06:09.148 --> 00:06:11.086
It teaches you to have drive.

00:06:11.086 --> 00:06:13.339
When you don't have a machine behind you,

00:06:13.339 --> 00:06:17.506
that's when, you know, that
God-given drive comes out.

00:06:18.774 --> 00:06:22.584
And sometimes when you
have a machine too early,

00:06:22.584 --> 00:06:26.524
you just kind of, you know,
become dependent on it,

00:06:26.524 --> 00:06:29.561
and when that machine goes away,

00:06:29.561 --> 00:06:32.193
you find artists that
don't even know how to live

00:06:32.193 --> 00:06:35.993
or function without a major backing.

00:06:35.993 --> 00:06:38.993
So I cherished the independent days.

00:06:40.043 --> 00:06:43.363
I'm about to embark on a
new journey with a major,

00:06:43.363 --> 00:06:44.215
and I'm excited.

00:06:44.215 --> 00:06:46.125
I think it's time.

00:06:46.125 --> 00:06:47.825
- [Interviewer] Do you read the blogs?

00:06:47.825 --> 00:06:49.955
- I don't read them.
- No? Okay.

00:06:49.955 --> 00:06:53.014
- Anything about me,
really I don't read them.

00:06:53.014 --> 00:06:55.186
Even if there's an
article somewhere about me

00:06:55.186 --> 00:06:59.173
and people call me and
tell me, I won't read them.

00:06:59.173 --> 00:07:02.090
It puts you in the mind frame of...

00:07:04.105 --> 00:07:05.765
A victim too much.

00:07:05.765 --> 00:07:10.403
And when you're a powerful
person, you can't play victim.

00:07:10.403 --> 00:07:12.315
Ya know, victim has to go out the door.

00:07:12.315 --> 00:07:14.725
When you read negative things,
you feel sorry for yourself,

00:07:14.725 --> 00:07:16.731
and there's no room in life
to feel sorry for yourself.

00:07:16.731 --> 00:07:18.741
It's just like, yo, let's go.

00:07:18.741 --> 00:07:21.186
You have to be a beast.

00:07:21.186 --> 00:07:23.487
That's the only way they respect you.

00:07:23.487 --> 00:07:25.320
I came up under Wayne,

00:07:26.178 --> 00:07:29.311
and Wayne has his way of doing things.

00:07:29.311 --> 00:07:31.528
When Wayne walks on the
(language censored) set

00:07:31.528 --> 00:07:34.501
and say, "Don't talk to me.

00:07:34.501 --> 00:07:36.831
"Have my (language censored) music ready.

00:07:36.831 --> 00:07:37.748
"Get the (language
censored) up out of my face,

00:07:37.748 --> 00:07:39.288
"and I'ma blow this (language censored)

00:07:39.288 --> 00:07:42.184
"in your face all day," it's cool.

00:07:42.184 --> 00:07:46.244
But every time I put my foot
down and stand up for myself,

00:07:46.244 --> 00:07:49.681
